A simple video game code for educational purposes could be something like this:

```
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {
    string name;
    int age;
    int score;

    cout << "Enter your name: ";
    getline(cin, name);

    cout << "Enter your age: ";
    cin >> age;

    cout << "Enter your score: ";
    cin >> score;

    cout << "Hello, " << name << "! You are " << age << " years old and have a score of " << score << "." << endl;

    return 0;
}
```

This code would prompt the user to enter their name, age, and score, and then output a message to the user. The code would be simple and easy to understand, and could be used as a starting point for more complex video game code.
